---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageMetadataTool from '../components/ImageMetadataTool.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
const schemas = [
  {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication',name:'ConvertAnyFile Image Metadata Viewer',url:`${SITE.origin}/image-metadata/`,applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication',operatingSystem:'Any',isAccessibleForFree:true,offers:{'@type':'Offer',price:'0',priceCurrency:'USD'},featureList:['View image metadata locally','Inspect profile names and image attributes','Remove metadata from a new image copy','Optionally preserve ICC or ICM color profile','JPG, PNG and WebP support','No source-image upload']},
  {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:`${SITE.origin}/`},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Image Tools',item:`${SITE.origin}/image-tools/`},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:'Image Metadata',item:`${SITE.origin}/image-metadata/`}]},
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Image Metadata Viewer & Remover Online | ConvertAnyFile" description="View image metadata locally in your browser and create a metadata-cleaned JPG, PNG or WebP copy. Inspect profiles and attributes, optionally preserve the color profile, and avoid source-image uploads." schema={schemas} noindex>
<section class="converter-page-hero image-tool-page-hero"><div class="site-container converter-page-hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs converter-page-breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/image-tools/">Image Tools</a><span>/</span><span>Image Metadata</span></div><span class="eyebrow converter-page-eyebrow">Metadata · Preview</span><h1>View and remove image metadata locally</h1><p>Inspect metadata profiles and attributes from a JPG, PNG or WebP image in your browser. If you choose to clean it, the tool creates a new encoded copy and can preserve the ICC/ICM color profile.</p></div></section>
<section class="image-tool-page-tool"><div class="site-container"><ImageMetadataTool /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">What the viewer shows</span><h2>See metadata before deciding whether to remove it.</h2><p>The viewer surfaces ImageMagick-detected profile names and readable image attributes locally. Depending on the source, those can include EXIF-related values, comments, software tags, XMP/IPTC-style profiles, color profiles, or nothing at all.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Cleaner caveat</strong><p>Metadata cleaning writes a new image file. For lossy formats such as JPG that means a new encoding generation, so this tool does not claim byte-for-byte or pixel-for-pixel identity with the source. Keep important originals.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Color profiles</span><h2>Preserve the display profile by default.</h2><p>ICC and ICM profiles can affect color appearance. The cleaner keeps those profiles by default while removing other detected metadata. Turn the option off only when you deliberately want a more aggressive metadata-cleaned copy.</p></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="/bulk-rename-images/">Bulk Rename Images <span>→</span></a><a class="related-card" href="/compress-image/">Compress Image <span>→</span></a><a class="related-card" href="/image-tools/">All Image Tools <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
